Practice: Will this compile? If not, give two ways to fix it.

public class Outer {
    class Inner { }
    public static void main(String[] args) {
        Inner i = new Inner();
    }
}

Step 1: Inner is a non-static inner class, so every Inner object needs an enclosing Outer object.
Step 2: main is static, so there is no this (no Outer object) to attach it to.
Step 3: javac reports: non-static variable this cannot be referenced from a static context.

Answer: it does **not compile**. Fix 1: Inner i = new Outer().new Inner(); Fix 2: declare it as **static class Inner**, then new Inner() works.

