Practice: Find the output.

import java.util.*;

public class ListOps {
    public static void main(String[] args) {
        List<Integer> list = new ArrayList<>();
        list.add(10);
        list.add(20);
        list.add(30);
        list.add(1, 15);
        list.remove(Integer.valueOf(10));
        list.remove(0);
        System.out.println(list + " size=" + list.size());
    }
}

Step 1: after three add calls the list is [10, 20, 30].
Step 2: add(1, 15) inserts at index 1: [10, 15, 20, 30].
Step 3: remove(Integer.valueOf(10)) removes the object 10 (by value): [15, 20, 30].
Step 4: remove(0) with an int removes by index 0: [20, 30].

Answer: **[20, 30] size=2**

